 "verdict": "The relative masses do not fit. The executed model gives every quark of all three generations one rest phase and every lepton another; the right-handed electron gets zero and the neutrino gets the electron's value. With the electron as anchor the up and down quarks come out within a factor 1.4 and 3; every other particle misses by factors of 20 to 100,000, and the neutrinos by more than a million. If the masses fitted, every particle would need the same tick; they need ticks spread over five orders of magnitude."
